                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One game mode, six maps, $10 USD.  Not Early Access.  The developer considers this a finished product, and the publisher, well, one look at their catalogue shows that they don't care either way.\n\nShoot other tanks, try not to get shot.  Whoever has the highest score when the time runs out wins.  Woop-dee-shit.\n\nOf the six maps, only the Eridani Strike one is any good, as it has NPC tanks to make things interesting.  That is unless you're playing with bots, as the AI has no concept of the game's objectives beyond \"shoot things\", which makes the game absurdly easy to win.\n\nDefinitely give [i]Battletank LOBA[/i] a pass.  It is worth neither your time, your money, nor your hard drive space.",
